invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_field.c
catches: p384_equiv_test
reason: the modular sum subtracts the modulus when the low 384 bits
  are at or above it and not when the sum carried out of them, so (m -
  1) + (m - 1) keeps 2^384 too little. bin/p384_equiv_test adds the
  edges of each modulus to each other.

--- old
    uint64_t carry = p384_wide_add_raw(o, a, b);
    if (carry || p384_wide_compare(o, mod->m) >= 0) {
--- new
    (void)p384_wide_add_raw(o, a, b);
    if (p384_wide_compare(o, mod->m) >= 0) {
